==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|VL.|-}} {{m|la|scōpa||broom}} (Latin {{m|la|scōpae||twigs, broom}} ). Compare {{cog|es|escoba||broom}}.

[[File:Dasypoda,f, united kingdom, side 2014-10-11-20.33.26 ZS PMax (15554938239).jpg|thumb|Large scopae on the hind legs of ''Dasypoda sp.'' bee]]

====Noun====
{{en-noun|scopae}}

# Any of various clusters of hair of non-[[parasitic]] [[bee]]s that serve to [[carry]] [[pollen]]. In parasitic {{taxfmt|Hymenoptera|order}} it refers to a local patch of hairs, regardless of function.

===Etymology 2===
Borrowed from {{uder|en|it|-}}.

